crosec: annotate ec_command_bytemuck where its response is discarded

cargo reports these four call sites as "code that will be rejected by a future
version of Rust": they depend on never type fallback being (), which becomes a
hard error in Rust 2024 and eventually in all editions. crosec is edition 2021
so this is a slow fuse rather than a break today - but it is a break that
arrives with no change to this repository, on the fix pkexec authenticates
against under the GUI, and therefore on a restore.

Upstream cannot supply the fix: ChocolateLoverRaj/crosec-rs origin/main is
still exactly b67daa7, the pinned commit, with no commits since. Bumping the
pin would change nothing.

The annotation is the compiler's own suggestion, and upstream already uses the
pattern where the response is kept - hello.rs reads
ec_command_bytemuck::<_, EcResponseHello>(. These five calls discard it, so the
output type is spelled () rather than left to fallback.

Five, not the four cargo listed: ec_cmd_set_fan_target_rpm discards a response
in both arms of its match, and only the first was reported. Annotating just the
reported one would leave the same defect in the same function to be found again
later.

